      {
        "id": "p17-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If $AD=6\\text{ cm}$, $DB=4\\text{ cm}$ and $AE=7\\text{ cm}$, calculate AC.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$AC=\\dfrac{60}{7}\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "Since $AB=AD+DB=6+4=10\\text{ cm}$, corresponding sides in $\\triangle ADE\\sim\\triangle ACB$ give $\\frac{AD}{AC}=\\frac{AE}{AB}$. Thus $\\frac{6}{AC}=\\frac{7}{10}$, so $AC=\\frac{60}{7}\\text{ cm}$.",
